package cajeta.xpu.core;

/**
 * Storage format of a {@link Texture2D}. Selects how texels are stored on the
 * device (channel count + per-channel encoding); a `Texture2D.sample(...)`
 * always returns a `Vector<float32, 4>` regardless — the hardware sampler
 * expands missing channels (G/B = 0, A = 1) and decodes the stored encoding to
 * float.
 *
 * Two independent axes are folded into one format:
 *   - **channels:** 1 (R) or 4 (RGBA).
 *   - **encoding:** 32-bit float (the value is read back as-is, any range), or
 *     8-bit UNORM (a byte 0..255 stored, read back normalized to float [0, 1] —
 *     the common, compact color-texture encoding).
 *
 * `upload(float32[])` always takes channel-interleaved floats in [0, 1] for the
 * UNORM formats (quantized to bytes on store) or any range for the float
 * formats; the runtime owns the float → storage encoding.
 *
 * **Ordinal values are the stable native contract** — the
 * `__cajeta_xpu_texture_*` intrinsics (see
 * [`runtime/native/cajeta_runtime.c`](../../../native/cajeta_runtime.c)) switch
 * on them to pick the per-backend image format (`VK_FORMAT_*`, HIP
 * `hipChannelFormatDesc`, CPU storage). Do **not** reorder without updating that
 * C side. Raw-integer (non-normalized, int-returning) textures are a separate
 * `fetch` surface and are intentionally not in this enum.
 */
public enum TextureFormat {
    R32F,         // 0 — 1 channel, 32-bit float           (VK_FORMAT_R32_SFLOAT)
    R8_UNORM,     // 1 — 1 channel, 8-bit normalized [0,1]  (VK_FORMAT_R8_UNORM)
    RGBA8_UNORM,  // 2 — 4 channel, 8-bit normalized [0,1]  (VK_FORMAT_R8G8B8A8_UNORM)
    RGBA32F       // 3 — 4 channel, 32-bit float            (VK_FORMAT_R32G32B32A32_SFLOAT)
}
